{"id":"word:hebrew:H5321","type":"word","title":"נַפְתָּלִי","subtitle":"H5321 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Naphtali , a son of Jacob, with the tribe descended from him, and its territory","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נַפְתָּלִי (H5321) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m n-pr-loc.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 51 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נַפְתָּלִי (Naphtâlîy) means Naphtali , a son of Jacob, with the tribe descended from him, and its territory First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נַפְתָּלִי","transliteration":"Naphtâlîy","pronunciation":"naf-taw-lee'","strong":"H5321","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5321","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m n-pr-loc","forms":["נַפְתָּלִ֖י","נַפְתָּלִ֑י","נַפְתָּלִ֔י","נַפְתָּלִ֗י","נַפְתָּלִֽי"],"morphs":[["HNp",39],["HC/Np",5],["HR/Np",4],["HC/R/Np",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"Naphtali , a son of Jacob, with the tribe descended from him, and its territory","usage":"Naphtali.","full":"H5321. Naphtali נַפְתָּלִי proper name, masculine and of a tribe Naphtali , Νεφθαλει ( μ ), etc. (interpreted as my wrestling Gen 30:8 ; perhaps originally crafty, cunning one ); — 1 second son of Jacob and Bilhah Gen 30:8 (J), 35:25 ; 46:24 (P), 1Chr 2:2 , compare Gen 49:21 (poem). 2 as a tribe of Israel: a. Judg 1:33 ; 4:10 ; 5:18 ; Deut 33:23 (twice in verse) +; so (Hexateuch, only P) נ ׳בְּנֵי Judg 4:6 ; Num 1:42 6 t., נ ׳מַטֵּה 2:29 ; 1Kin 7:14 5 t., נ בְּנֵי ׳מַטֵּה Num 10:27 ; 34:28 ; Josh 19:39 ; נ ׳שַׁעַר Ezek 48:34 (in new Jerusalem); נ ׳אֶרֶץ 1Kin 15:20 ; 2Kin 15:29 , compare Isaiah 8:23; נ ׳קֶדֶשׁ Judg 4:6 ; נ ׳הַר Josh 20:7 ; נ ׳גְּבוּל Ezek 48:4 , נ ׳יָ֫מָּה 48:3 ; נ ׳עָרֵי 2Chr 16:4 . b. as territorial name Deut 34:2 (JE) 1Kin 4:15 ; 1 Chronicles 12:41 (van d. H. v. 1Chr 12:40 ), 2Chr 34:6 ; Judg 6:35 ; 7:23 might be a or b.","rootNote":"from 6617 ; my wrestling;","sources":["Morph